CODEGEN.md §2.4, WIRE.md §6.5 (DECISIONS 341): a `load.dir` glob matching a data file an emit of the same build writes is refused at the load under `canon build`, and nothing is written.
-- project.canon --
project acme {
  canon: "0.1"
}
-- a/a.canon --
/// A.
package a

/// V.
let v: Int = 1

emit json { out: "out/" }
-- b/b.canon --
/// B.
package b

/// R.
record R {
  /// The value.
  v: Int
}

/// All.
let all: [R] = load.dir("../a/out/*.json")
-- a/out/v.json --
{"v": 1}
-- findings.txt --
error[E8026]  b/b.canon:11:16
  a/out/v.json is read by this load and written by emit json of a: an output is never an input of its own build

1 error, 0 warnings in 2 packages (…)
